id: pm-distribution-consumer-lease
title: Protect distribution inventory and staging from concurrent dist rebuilds
description: "The distribution packer reads the live dist tree outside the shared build/test lease. During this delivery an overlapping linked-test rebuild caused npm pack --dry-run to fail with ENOENT for a dist/cli-bundle/chunks file; packing passed when rerun after the rebuild settled. Existing completed producer/test-consumer serialization and physical runtime staging remain valid, but this additional packing consumer is not protected."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-10T19:46:26.278Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T15:32:01.354Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-12T15:32:00.744Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-12T15:32:00.744Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Hold a verified consumer lease or equivalent immutable generation throughout source inventory and staging; use real independent build/pack overlap to prove no missing or mixed-generation files; retain fail-closed incomplete-generation handling and existing physical-path guards; do not replace ownership evidence with timer-only fixtures or force lock overrides.
value: Reliable context and release evidence requires packed consumers to use a consistent tested generation.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Lease complete distribution packing; scope inherited tokens to a resolvable matching workspace, otherwise acquire independent ownership; preserve live-token and incomplete-generation validation."
expected_result: "Concurrent rebuilds never produce mixed artifacts, and deleted or invalid inherited owner paths cannot block unrelated valid workspaces or authorize token reuse."
actual_result: "Real independent producer/packer contention and its lease-removal negative control pass. Both deleted and non-directory owner regressions fail before the review fix and pass afterward. All 52 packing/ownership assertions and all three linked command groups pass, with invalid matching tokens and original owner/file bytes preserved. Structured production-defect gate evidence is now complete; final exact-head native/coverage checks are required before merge."
