comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T19:46:26.278Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: the strict 2920-item all-status corpus plus the newly created qualification child and request-specific search found no focused distribution-consumer lease report. Full live reads confirm pm-cxc4jc completed producer/test-consumer serialization and pm-gh1417 completed runtime staging. This distinct consumer boundary was observed as ENOENT during overlapping verification and passes once serialized; it remains open and unclaimed for implementation under the existing release capability."
  "2026-10-12T09:52:31.603Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: extend the existing verified build-consumer lease across publication source inventory and materialization, reject incomplete build generations, and preserve physical-path/runtime ledger admission. Prove serialization with independent real build/pack processes and ownership barriers rather than time-based overlap assumptions."
  "2026-10-12T10:14:30.874Z","harness:codex","Independent real-process acceptance passes: actual build.mjs runs owned fixture stages while the separate packer proves EEXIST contention against that live PID/token, then both archive files equal generation two. An isolated copy with only withBuildLease removed fails this exact assertion. Incomplete-build and invalid inherited-token controls preserve their marker/owner bytes; existing runtime-ledger,physical-path,lossless-JSON and Windows launcher tests pass. Base package budget remains unchanged at19908805 first-party bytes and1658 files; runtime closure23387074 bytes/4745 files."
  "2026-10-12T10:54:37.467Z","harness:codex","Broad verification caught the new packer import missing from preserved release controls. The reviewed release workflow now copies build-lease beside temp-lifecycle, and native foreign-workspace execution passes. Further independent ownership tests reproduced and repaired ambient-token reuse in a foreign cwd: runners now carry an explicit physical workspace binding, legacy tokens use the script workspace, foreign roots acquire independent leases, valid nested reads retain the original owner bytes, and invalid matching-root tokens still refuse. Isolated pre-fix run fails5 exact assertions/119 passes; identical repaired source passes182. Integrated Node24 regression passes220 assertions across8 files,including CI directory-density and the approved Sentry declaration pin."
  "2026-10-12T11:33:17.249Z","harness:codex","The new workspace-bound lease metadata must not expose its source path or reusable token to snapshot/isolated linked commands. A native child probe demonstrates the pre-fix leak (true:false:false:true:true instead of true:false:false:false:false). SDK execution now removes both controls for non-source modes, and stored environment directives reserve both names. This is part of the introduced lease protocol, not a claim that the older completed source-context delivery was unimplemented."
  "2026-10-12T11:35:53.274Z","harness:codex",The same strengthened native mode test now passes after source lease token+root removal from snapshot/isolated children. Existing source execution retains its host lease controls; both names are reserved from stored env-set/env-clear directives. Focused SDK/transport/packing checks pass88 assertions. The final full suite uses the verified absolute Node24.21.0 executable with its bundled npm; prior shell-selected Node26 runs are retained as unsuccessful evidence and not reused as coverage proof.
  "2026-10-12T15:05:12.901Z","harness:codex","Verified implementation head 7411d7ee6e29b288eba2b7222e294a31d74635fc: CI run 38264143222 is successful, all 26 required contexts are present and passed, GitHub merge state is CLEAN, and no inline review threads remain. Accepted CodeRabbit release-summary feedback is corrected. Sourcery/Cubic limits and the expired Greptile trial are availability limitations, not approvals. Closure and the latest package-generated changelog remain in the reviewed final push."
  "2026-10-12T15:27:50.934Z","harness:codex","Both terminal defect-gate findings belong to this item: escape_class and gate_evidence were absent at the first closure. Reopened and claimed the same canonical owner, supplied the production-defect classification and structured independently strengthened boundary evidence through PM, and preserved the prior close event. The valid CodeRabbit issue is separate: a deleted or non-directory inherited workspace path must not prevent independent packing of a valid root; matching live-token validation must remain fail-closed."
  "2026-10-12T15:30:42.054Z","harness:codex","Independent missing-owner and non-directory-owner cases both fail before the review fix with ENOENT/ENOTDIR. The repaired helper acquires independent ownership for those valid roots, releases only its own lease and preserves the unrelated file; all 52 distribution/ownership assertions pass, including matched invalid-token refusal, incomplete-marker preservation, real build overlap and live parent receipt retention. No lock override or ownership-validation bypass is added."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:16:52.147Z","harness:codex",An artifact consumer must retain producer ownership across source inventory and staging. Verify overlap with live PID/token contention and independent processes; file-copy completion or sleeps alone do not establish a consistent generation.
